# C6 final — CPU Flash vector compatibility at ubatch64

**Result: `COMPAT_NOT_RECOVERED_NEXT_DIVERGENCE`.** The one scoped CPU dispatch patch selected the intended existing vector path, preserved original output with the option OFF, left ub32 and decode fixtures unchanged, and removed the C5 layer0 CPU Flash difference on the physical target. It did **not** recover bitwise full-model parity for ubatch64. The next first difference is native GPU `ggml_flash_attn_ext` at layer29, absolute token48, output feature64. Same-input native CUDA replays reproduce both target outputs bitwise; regrouping the second32 queries as 32 recovers the ub32 output. This is a local native shape effect, not evidence of a streaming read/routing defect. No second functional patch, qualified prefill A/B, 496/1522 extension or sustained run followed. Conservative ub32, no preload remains unchanged.

## Identity and boundary

Frozen protocol `C6-PROTOCOL-20260927.md`; chronological ledger `C6-LEDGER-20260927.md`. Lab branch `campaign/c6-attn-dispatch-compat-20260927-0301utc` from C5 `9426492db4faeb3f5765af24938bd4fb4d8708f6`. Original backend `1248fd8fa8cfebaece5ea992e4d951c1e18bb9d5` and its build were preserved. Separate backend worktree/branch at `backends/streaming-c6-attn-compat`, one patch commit `c4104706a123ea92fb47bfab9a1f95a4e6cf106d`; separate GCC15.3.1/Release/CUDA13.3 arch89 build. Original and patched probes have distinct RUNPATH and loaded-library hashes in every monitored manifest. No model, quantization, top-k, KV, mask, output policy, sampler, CPU/GPU map or weights changed. Target GGUF SHA-256 `582bd40f6886200101f4c4ed9f25f3fe80cc14c86e9e2b37746cd8904a0c622d` (63,387,346,208 B); exact 113-ID TSV SHA-256 `368c48ac1e93d68ec1746bb3d5f7e63118f35d7903c58f88dbe5c983b69190fb`.

**SOURCE_AUDITED / REPRODUZIDO_MODEL_FREE:** The patch parses `TESY_CPU_FA_PREFILL_VEC_COMPAT` once at CPU backend initialization (absent OFF, exactly `1` ON, other present values abort). Only original tiled F32-Q/F16-KV/F16-mask CPU Flash prefill with `nq>=64` and checked native row layout changes to the existing vector implementation. The predicate does not set global `use_ref`, alter workspace planning or touch CUDA. The existing workspace reserves the larger prefill/decode maximum. Native captured-input bridges: patched OFF A32 and B64 match C5 normal outputs; ON A32 is unchanged; ON B64 matches the full C5 B64 `use_ref` output and its first32 rows match A32. Model-free n_query31/32/63/64/65 and F32-KV/decode n_query1 with nkv256/512 confirm only in-scope F16 prefill changes. Invalid mode, missing/truncated/nonfinite source, overwrite and absent scratch fail closed. Relevant prior comparator/gate tests passed 41/41 and the delayed-work C4 clock test passed. `results/c6-d1-local-summary02.json` is the sealed local gate. The earlier `summary01` is a preserved analyzer-only FAIL from a mistyped expected patch SHA.

## MEDIDO_NO_TARGET: decisive 113-ID run

All six arms used one external batch of exactly113 tokens, b256, ctx4096, GPU8 actual CPU0–28/GPU29–35, slots32, threads8/I/O4, O_DIRECT/no repack, `op_offload=false`, preload OFF, final-token-only logits mask and separate fresh processes. Every arm had memory.max18GiB/swap.max0, RSS17GiB, GPU7000MiB, MemAvailable6GiB, CPU/GPU/NVMe95/80/70°C, timeout300 and sampled telemetry. Six runs completed without a stop, swap, cgroup max/OOM event, corruption or nonfinite output. These are **one-shot diagnostic clocks**, not a performance comparison; the option had not passed full-model equality.

| Arm / run ID prefix `c6-d2-` | ubatch / build / mode | Full logits SHA-256 | Completed prefill, s |
|---|---|---|---:|
| `a0-original32-short01` | 32 original OFF | `8ba19722…285` | 42.789120 |
| `a-patched32-off-short01` | 32 patched OFF | same A0 | 43.180997 |
| `aplus-patched32-on-short01` | 32 patched ON | same A0 | 43.316499 |
| `b-patched64-off-short01` | 64 patched OFF | `db4f1104…c36` (C5 B0) | 39.582531 |
| `c1-patched64-on-short01` | 64 patched ON | `153c5ab6…12a` | 39.624904 |
| `c2-patched64-on-short01` | 64 patched ON | same C1 | 38.924651 |

A0=A=A+ bitwise; B reproduces historical B0 bitwise; C1=C2 bitwise. C/A+ still differs in **201087/201088** F32 logits, maximum absolute delta **0.2306489944**, RMSE **0.0448836917**. The known B/A+ delta was larger (max1.5265813, RMSE0.2294881), but C's smaller delta is not parity. Thus `FULL_MODEL_COMPAT_SHORT_PASS` fails and the performance gate is closed. A separate diagnostic target witness with `TESY_CPU_FA_DISPATCH_TRACE=1` preserved C1 logits bitwise and logged 29 CPU `nq64` invocations with `selected=1 branch=vector`, plus 29 tail `nq49` invocations on the original vector branch. Its timing is excluded. See `results/c6-d2-dispatch-witness01.json`.

## MEDIDO_NO_TARGET + native replay: next first difference

Five capture pairs (CPU layer0 attention, all layer outputs, GPU29 coarse operations, GPU29 Q/K/V/Flash, and GPU29 Flash sources) were each final-logit neutral within A+ and C. Logical rows were aligned by absolute token rather than internal chunk number; valid zero-row last-layer chunks were handled. CPU layer0 attention and its Q/K/V/RoPE/Flash output agreed for all113 positions; all layer outputs 0–28 agreed. GPU29 `attn_norm` and Q/K/V projections, reshapes and RoPE agreed for all113. The **first different observed operation is GPU29 Flash Attention at token48/feature64**, max absolute Flash delta0.01494026 over all its observed rows. `attn_out` first differs at token48/feature0, then FFN and layer output. Layer29 output is equal at 56/113 positions and first differs at token48/feature0. These are operation-order observations, not a claim that every internal CUDA instruction was inspected.

GPU29 Flash sources at A+ chunk1 (tokens32–63) and C chunk0 (tokens0–63) have exact matching Q and mask for corresponding tokens32–63 and exact K/V/sinks bytes. Captured types/strides are Q F32 `[64,nq,64]`, K/V F16 `[64,256,8]`, F16 mask `[256,nq]`, F32 sinks `[64]`; `flash_sources.tsv` and every payload were shape/byte checked. An isolated native GGML CUDA replay, without streaming or model loading, reproduced A32 captured Flash output SHA `7b2e4f9e…b09fe` and C64 captured Flash output SHA `285a514e…4ae96` bitwise. On the **same C input**, replaying only the second32 queries with their exact mask rows and complete common KV returned the A32 bytes; C64's second32 rows differed in 36861/131072 F32 values, first at token48/feature64, max absolute0.00334549. This controlled grouping intervention demonstrates a native CUDA shape effect at this operation and explains the next target origin in the tested case. It does not decompose every subsequent full-model delta.

**SOURCE_AUDITED / INFERIDO:** Pinned `ggml-cuda/fattn.cu` dispatch can select CUDA MMA Flash on this Ada device for F32 Q/F16 KV and these shapes. The precise runtime kernel symbol and launch geometry were not profiled; do not claim a specific specialization as measured. Neither CPU nor GPU vector path is asserted more accurate. There is no second patch to GPU Flash in C6.

## Resources, audit and decision

Across 17 monitored C6 model runs (six controls/candidates, ten neutral captures, one dispatch witness), highest cgroup memory.peak was 14,686,404,608 B; highest sampled RSS 14,840,414,208 B; GPU3882 MiB/56°C, CPU86.375°C, NVMe52.85°C, runtime swap0. Native CUDA replays had no model process and completed under the same cgroup cap; their subsecond sample cadence is not used as sustained telemetry. Host swap used by unrelated processes was not touched. Source/raw/capture hashes in the compact summaries are **post-run seals**, not attestation at capture time.

Authority: `results/c6-d2-short-diagnostic-summary03.json` with strict manifest, binary/library, model/input, row/output and resource checks; `summary01` is a preserved analyzer SHA typo FAIL, `summary02` is an earlier passing but less strict source-index version. Large raw tensors, logs, `.f32` files, model and builds remain local/untracked. The backend patch, small replay/observer scripts, protocol, ledger, final, index and compact reports are the review unit. At campaign close, no remote push, PR, CI, merge or default change had been performed. No performance confirmation, 496/1522 extension, teacher-forced decode target, sustained service or waves measurement was run. `BROAD_NOVELTY_NO_GO / ENGINEERING_AND_MEASUREMENT_GO`.

**GitHub review packaging (later user-authorized publication):** `research/patches/C6-cpu-flash-vector-compat.patch` is the exact `git format-patch` export of backend commit `c4104706a123ea92fb47bfab9a1f95a4e6cf106d` against pin `1248fd8fa8cfebaece5ea992e4d951c1e18bb9d5`; patch SHA-256 `196ec080bb06298ec820c4775064a1950a9b2bc920ea489bead154e60f3581e8`. `git apply --check` passed against the preserved original backend worktree. The Tesy C6 branch is the publication unit; the upstream backend remote is not a publication target. Raw evidence and model/build products remain local.

Effective tested commands are recorded without abbreviation in every `results/c6-d2*.json` manifest. Local gates were run with `PYTHONPATH=tools python3 -m unittest tools.test_c5_compare tools.test_c2_gate tools.test_c3_approval tools.test_c3_terminal_sample`, `tools/test_c4_prefill_clock`, `tools/c6_flash_replay A32|B64 normal OUTPUT`, `TESY_CPU_FA_PREFILL_VEC_COMPAT=1 tools/c6_flash_replay A32|B64 normal OUTPUT`, `tools/c6_flash_dispatch_fixture NQ NKV f16|f32 OUTPUT`, `PYTHONPATH=tools python3 tools/c6_check_local.py`, `tools/c6_gpu29_flash_replay A32|C64|C32second normal OUTPUT`, `PYTHONPATH=tools python3 tools/c6_compare_d2.py`, and `PYTHONPATH=tools python3 tools/c6_check_trace.py`. Each 120B arm used `systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=19327352832 -p MemorySwapMax=0 -- python3 tools/run_bounded.py` with the frozen resource flags above and its manifest's exact binary, environment and run ID.

Next decision: retain the conservative profile. A future campaign may qualify a **single, prospectively specified GPU Flash numerical/dispatch compatibility test** or accept native64 only under a separately frozen numerical and sampling contract. C6 authorizes neither intervention nor a default switch.
